  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Human Rights Association Istanbul Branch</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The cooperation aims to contribute to increased democratization by disclosing obstacles to democracy. This is done by increasing public sensitivity to issues related to democracy, raising awareness in the society by sharing reports about individuals and institutions exposed to rights violations, and influencing decision makers and legislators. The purpose of Human Rights Association&apos;s branch operating in Istanbul is to carry out studies about all human right&apos;s violations that occur in Istanbul but also to support victims of violations and advocate for change. The Asscociation branch&apos;s priority areas are violationes of fundamental rights and freedoms, torture and ill-treatment in custody and prisons, enforced disapperance and intrusion of privacy/spying, inability to access justice mechanisms, harm in a conflict environment, violance and abuse against women and children, poverty, rights violations in the workplace, refugees, LGBTQ tights, freedom of expression, women, children, forced displacement and environmental issues.</narrative>
  </description>
